cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "regime-hmm: A from-scratch Gaussian HMM for honest market-regime characterization"
abstract: >-
  A pure, typed Python implementation of a Gaussian Hidden Markov Model for
  market-regime characterization — emission log-density, log-space
  forward-backward, Baum-Welch EM with seeded restarts, Viterbi, and an online
  forward filter — parity-tested to 1e-6 against hmmlearn. The online forward
  filter (data up to t only) is the sole tradable regime signal; smoothed and
  Viterbi posteriors peek ahead and are exploratory-only. A regime-conditioned
  exposure overlay is tested out-of-sample against buy-and-hold under realistic
  per-side costs, with a pure-function verdict that is structurally unable to
  claim a timing edge unless the Memmel-corrected Jobson-Korkie Sharpe-difference
  test is significant and the Deflated Sharpe (with the full effective number of
  trials) survives. The honest finding is that regime characterization is the
  deliverable; the timing overlay does not reliably beat buy-and-hold after costs
  and its in-sample edge decays under deflation.
